/*  FILE:  PROOFER.MNE

/*  Table of transcription mnemonics  --  January, 1997

/*  Purpose of table:
/*            1. provides the list of legal mnemonics in
/*               the manuscript, and
/*            2. instructs PROOFER in the parsing of
/*               the mnemonics and their textual components.

/*  Instructions for coding the processing of mnemonics:

/*     Position of mnemonic:
/*        1    mnemonic must be within column mnemonic
/*        2    mnemonic must be outside column mnemonic
/*        3    mnemonic can occur anywhere

/*     Contents of mnemonic:
/*        1    mnemonic must not have text
/*        2    mnemonic must have text
/*        3    mnemonic must have inserted text
/*        4    mnemonic may or may not have text
/*        5    mnemonic must have remark

/*        Note:  Any mnemonic can have comments.

/*         The mnemonic must be in the first column and the
/*         first character of the mnemonic must be an open
/*         brace '{'.  The code for the position of the
/*         mnemonic and the contents of the mnemonic must
/*         be in columns 2 and 3, respectively.

/* General processing:
/*        1.  mnemonic cannot be within []
/*        2.  mnemonic cannot be within ()
/*        3.  mnemonic must be closed before end of column boundary
/*        4.  any mnemonic continued must have " +" before ending "}"
/*        5.  any mnemonic must be followed by
/*               "." (except for remarks mnemonic)
/*                  - or - 
/*               ":"
/*                  - or - 
/*               "1" thru "9" (for column boundary,
/*                             headword, initial mnemonics)
/*                  - or - 
/*               "=" (for miniature and diagram mnemonics)
/*        6.  any mnemonic must be preceded by
/*               "{"
/*                  - or - 
/*               "{=" (for miniature and diagram mnemonics)
 
/* Special processing:

/* 0  No special processing

/* 1  Addendum and Gloss (currently {AD.} and {GL.})
/*    mnemonic must be immediately followed by space + [^ + text

/* 2  Blank (currently {BLNK.})
/*        no more than one blank mnemonic in a row

/* 3  Catchword (currently {CW.})
/*        must be on separate line
/*        must be after end of column boundary
/*       "[...]" can be after catchword, but not before

/* 4  Column Boundary (currently {CB.})

/* 5  Diagram (currently {DIAG.})
/*       bad format for "|"
/*           should be: |blah|blah|blah|}

/* 6  Headword (currently {HD.})

/* 7  Initial (currently {IN.})
/*       must be followed by space and capital letter;
/*         - or -
/*       must be followed by capital letter within (, (^, [, or [^
/*         - or -
/*       must be followed by miniature mnemonic

/* 8  Miniature (currently {MIN.})

/* 9  Remarks (currently {RMK.})
/*       can not be on a line by itself within text
/*       can be by itself at beginning of manuscript

/* 10 Rubric (currently {RUB.})

/* 11 Symbol (currently {SYMB.})

/* 12 Signature (currently {SG.})
/*        must be on separate line
/*        must be after end of column boundary
/*       "[...]" can be after catchword, but not before



/*********************************************************************************************************/

/*  Text descriptors:                   
/*  mnemonic            position      contents    can span   can       numbered      can have   special
/*                                                lines      continue                vectors    processing

     {BLNK                 1             1          N          N          N             N            2

     {CB                   3             4          Y          Y          Y             N            4

     {CW                   2             2          N          N          N             N            3
     
     {DIAG                 1             4          N          Y          N             Y            5

     {HD                   2             2          Y          Y          Y/N           N            6

     {IN                   1             1          N          N          Y             N            7

     {ILL                  1             4          Y          N          N             N            0
   
     {MIN                  1             4          Y          N          N             Y            8
     
     {RUB                  1             4          Y          Y          N             N           10

     {SYMB                 1             5          Y          N          N             N           11

     {SG                   2             2          N          N          N             N            3
     
/*  Scribal or editorial additions:
/*  mnemonic            position      contents    can span   can       numbered     can have     special
/*                                                lines      continue               vectors      processing

                                                                                                     
     {AD                   1             3          Y          Y           N             N           1

                                                                                                     
     {GL                   1             3          Y          Y           N             N           1

/*  Languages:
/*  mnemonic            position      contents    can span   can       numbered     can have     special
/*                                                lines      continue                vectors     processing


     {ARB                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {ARG                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {ARM                 1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {BAS                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {CAL                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {CAT                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {ENG                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {FRN                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {GAL                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {GER                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {GRK                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {HEB                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {ITL                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {LAM                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {LAT                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {PRT                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0
     {PRV                  1             2          Y          Y         N            N             0

/*  Remarks:
/*  mnemonic            position      contents    can span   can       numbered     can have    special
/*                                                lines      continue                vectors    processing

     {RMK                  3             5          Y          N         N            N             9





/* End of PROOFER.MNE
